# Simonethg deploy gate — confirmation before production

## Hard rule

**Do not** publish `packages/nextjs` (or any playground UI) to production, change DNS, create subdomains, or overwrite the live WordPress site until the usuaria confirms explicitly.

Confirmation phrases (examples — intent matters more than exact wording):

- “de acuerdo”
- “deployá” / “deploya” / “desplegá”
- “está listo” / “listo para producción”
- “publicá en simonethg.com”

Ambiguous “ok”, “dale”, or “sí” about *features* is **not** a deploy green light. If unclear, ask: “¿Confirmás deploy a producción en simonethg.com?”

## When she confirms

1. Deploy `packages/nextjs` so it is reachable under **www.simonethg.com** (or the path/subdomain she chose — see `docs/DEPLOY.md`).
2. Update the **root README** section **Para todos** with a clear public URL (prefer `https://www.simonethg.com/...` or the agreed playground path).
3. Keep in every README:

```markdown
**Powered by [AcademiaQA.com](https://academiaqa.com)**
```

4. Do **not** touch DNS or Hostinger WordPress root unless she explicitly asks for that option.

## Until then

- Local / preview only (`yarn nextjs:dev`, screenshots, localhost links in README).
- Commit rule/docs and app work freely; **no** production publish.

## Hosting snapshot (see `docs/DEPLOY.md`)

As of investigation: **simonethg.com** is **WordPress on Hostinger** (LiteSpeed, PHP). Apex is canonical; `www` redirects to apex. No Vercel project linked in this workspace. Path vs subdomain is **still to confirm** before first deploy.
